    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.02_typed_legs_and_atlas.sections.04_diagram_inventory_table.concrete_anchor_3#commacategory_joc_s340" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_02_typed_legs_and_atlas_sections_04_diagram_inventory_table_concrete_anchor_3#commacategory_joc_s340 silm:hasLongDescription "The CommaCategory_JoC_S340 is the comma category (F downarrow G) from JoC 3.40; instantiates Quantity vs. Observation non-identity. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'CommaCategory_JoC_S340', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
